{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-74604","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-105869","text":"Skill 01 — The Ten Protocols"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74606","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105870","text":"OS-001 through OS-010: what each protocol specifies, which product implements it, and the cognitive science behind it. Eight cognitive primitives plus two cross-cutting protocols (PRISM diagnostic, PULSE temporal)."}]}],"id":"blk-74605","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-74607","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-105871","text":"Overview"}]},{"id":"blk-74608","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105872","text":"OpenSentience publishes ten numbered protocols organized in two layers:"}]},{"id":"blk-74609","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74611","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105873","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive primitives (OS-001 — OS-008)"},{"id":"spn-105874","text":" — eight individual capabilities,"}]}],"id":"blk-74610","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74612","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105875","text":"each grounded in a cognitive science thread."}]},{"id":"blk-74613","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74615","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105876","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cross-cutting protocols (OS-009 PRISM, OS-010 PULSE)"},{"id":"spn-105877","text":" — two sibling"}]}],"id":"blk-74614","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74616","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105878","text":"protocols that sit above the cognitive primitives and above the [&] structural composition layer. PULSE declares how every loop in the ecosystem cycles, nests, and signals; PRISM measures how well those loops actually learn over time."}]},{"id":"blk-74617","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105879","text":"The protocols are independent specifications — they can be adopted individually or composed together. A system may publish a PULSE manifest without implementing any cognitive primitive, and PRISM can benchmark any PULSE-conforming system without bespoke per-system integration."}]},{"id":"blk-74618","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-105880","text":"OS-001: Continual Learning"}]},{"id":"blk-74619","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105881","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-105882","text":" Hippocampal consolidation (McClelland et al. 1995)"}]},{"id":"blk-74620","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105883","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74621","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74623","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105884","text":"Three node types: episodic (events), semantic (facts), procedural (workflows)"}]}],"id":"blk-74622","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74625","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105885","text":"Typed, weighted edges between nodes"}]}],"id":"blk-74624","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74627","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105886","text":"Confidence scores with evidence-calibrated assignment"}]}],"id":"blk-74626","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74629","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105887","text":"Consolidation cycle: decay low-confidence nodes, prune stale entries,"}]}],"id":"blk-74628","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74630","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105888","text":"merge near-duplicates, strengthen co-retrieved edges"}]},{"id":"blk-74631","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74633","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105889","text":"Memory timescales: working memory (session), short-term (hours), long-term"}]}],"id":"blk-74632","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74634","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105890","text":"(persistent)"}]},{"id":"blk-74635","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105891","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-105892","text":" New memories must be stored quickly (hippocampal fast-write) without disrupting existing knowledge (neocortical slow-consolidation). This maps to immediate ETS/SQLite writes with background consolidation."}]},{"id":"blk-74636","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105893","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-105894","text":" Graphonomous ("},{"id":"spn-105895","marks":["code"],"text":"store_node"},{"id":"spn-105896","text":", "},{"id":"spn-105897","marks":["code"],"text":"store_edge"},{"id":"spn-105898","text":", "},{"id":"spn-105899","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-105900","text":", "},{"id":"spn-105901","marks":["code"],"text":"run_consolidation"},{"id":"spn-105902","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-74637","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-105903","text":"OS-002: Topological Routing (kappa)"}]},{"id":"blk-74638","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105904","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-105905","text":" Working memory gating (O'Reilly & Frank 2006)"}]},{"id":"blk-74639","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105906","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74640","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74642","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105907","text":"The kappa parameter: a measure of cyclicity in a knowledge subgraph"}]}],"id":"blk-74641","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74644","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105908","text":"Strongly connected component (SCC) detection on retrieved neighborhoods"}]}],"id":"blk-74643","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74646","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105909","text":"Routing decision: kappa = 0 implies fast path (acyclic, no conflict),"}]}],"id":"blk-74645","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74647","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105910","text":"kappa > 0 implies deliberate path (cycles exist, may contain contradictions)"}]},{"id":"blk-74648","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74650","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105911","text":"Topological features: SCC count, max SCC size, edge density within cycles"}]}],"id":"blk-74649","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74651","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105912","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-105913","text":" The prefrontal cortex gates information into working memory based on relevance and conflict signals. Kappa serves as the conflict signal — cyclic knowledge regions indicate unresolved tension that requires deliberation before action."}]},{"id":"blk-74652","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105914","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-105915","text":" Graphonomous routing layer ("},{"id":"spn-105916","marks":["code"],"text":"topology_analyze"},{"id":"spn-105917","text":", "},{"id":"spn-105918","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-105919","text":" topology annotations)"}]},{"id":"blk-74653","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-105920","text":"OS-003: Deliberation Orchestrator"}]},{"id":"blk-74654","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105921","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-105922","text":" Dual-process theory (Kahneman 2011)"}]},{"id":"blk-74655","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105923","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74656","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74658","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105924","text":"Four-phase deliberation: bid, debate, vote, commit"}]}],"id":"blk-74657","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74660","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105925","text":"Argumentation framework: claims, warrants, rebuttals"}]}],"id":"blk-74659","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74662","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105926","text":"Consensus mechanisms: majority, supermajority, unanimity"}]}],"id":"blk-74661","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74664","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105927","text":"Timeout and escalation policies"}]}],"id":"blk-74663","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74666","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105928","text":"Triggered when kappa routing indicates deliberation is needed"}]}],"id":"blk-74665","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74667","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105929","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-105930","text":" System 1 (fast, automatic) handles routine decisions. System 2 (slow, deliberate) engages when conflict is detected. The kappa threshold is the trigger that shifts from fast to deliberate processing."}]},{"id":"blk-74668","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105931","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-105932","text":" AgenTroMatic ("},{"id":"spn-105933","marks":["code"],"text":"deliberate"},{"id":"spn-105934","text":" tool in Graphonomous provides the single-agent deliberation path)"}]},{"id":"blk-74669","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-105935","text":"OS-004: Attention Engine"}]},{"id":"blk-74670","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105936","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-105937","text":" Endogenous attention (Desimone & Duncan 1995)"}]},{"id":"blk-74671","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105938","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74672","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74674","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105939","text":"Three-phase cycle: survey (scan environment), triage (rank by salience),"}]}],"id":"blk-74673","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74675","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105940","text":"dispatch (act on highest-priority items)"}]},{"id":"blk-74676","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74678","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105941","text":"Salience scoring: combines urgency, recency, goal relevance, and confidence"}]}],"id":"blk-74677","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74680","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105942","text":"Goal bias: active goals increase salience of related knowledge"}]}],"id":"blk-74679","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74682","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105943","text":"Dispatch modes: act (execute), learn (gather more context), escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-74681","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74683","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105944","text":"(request human intervention), idle (nothing needed)"}]},{"id":"blk-74684","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105945","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-105946","text":" Biological attention is goal-directed (endogenous) not just stimulus-driven (exogenous). The attention engine prioritizes based on the agent's active goals, not just what is new or loud."}]},{"id":"blk-74685","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105947","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-105948","text":" Graphonomous attention module ("},{"id":"spn-105949","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_survey"},{"id":"spn-105950","text":", "},{"id":"spn-105951","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_run_cycle"},{"id":"spn-105952","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-74686","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-105953","text":"OS-005: Model Tier Adaptation"}]},{"id":"blk-74687","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105954","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-105955","text":" Resource rationality (Lieder & Griffiths 2020)"}]},{"id":"blk-74688","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105956","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74689","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74691","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105957","text":"Three tiers: "},{"id":"spn-105958","marks":["code"],"text":"local_small"},{"id":"spn-105959","text":" (8B parameter models), "},{"id":"spn-105960","marks":["code"],"text":"local_large"},{"id":"spn-105961","text":" (70B+),"}]}],"id":"blk-74690","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74692","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105962","marks":["code"],"text":"cloud_frontier"},{"id":"spn-105963","text":" (largest available)"}]},{"id":"blk-74693","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74695","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105964","text":"Same topology and tool surface at every tier — only depth and latency differ"}]}],"id":"blk-74694","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74697","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105965","text":"Escalation rules: when local_small confidence is below threshold, escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-74696","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74698","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105966","text":"to local_large; when local_large is insufficient, escalate to cloud_frontier"}]},{"id":"blk-74699","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74701","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105967","text":"Budget constraints: token limits, latency targets, cost caps per tier"}]}],"id":"blk-74700","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74702","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105968","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-105969","text":" Optimal cognition allocates computational resources proportional to decision importance. Simple decisions use fast/cheap processing; high-stakes decisions justify expensive computation."}]},{"id":"blk-74703","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105970","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-105971","text":" Graphonomous and Agentelic (tier selection and escalation logic)"}]},{"id":"blk-74704","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-105972","text":"OS-006: Agent Governance Shim"}]},{"id":"blk-74705","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105973","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-105974","text":" Executive function (Miyake et al. 2000)"}]},{"id":"blk-74706","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105975","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74707","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74709","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105976","text":"Permission taxonomy: filesystem, network, tool_invocation, graph_access"}]}],"id":"blk-74708","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74711","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105977","text":"Lifecycle state machine: installed, enabled, running, disabled, removed"}]}],"id":"blk-74710","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74713","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105978","text":"Graduated autonomy: observe, advise, act"}]}],"id":"blk-74712","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74715","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105979","text":"Append-only audit trail with typed events"}]}],"id":"blk-74714","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74717","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105980","text":"OTP-native implementation: GenStateMachine, ETS, DynamicSupervisor"}]}],"id":"blk-74716","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74718","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105981","marks":["bold"],"text":"Design constraint from cognitive science:"},{"id":"spn-105982","text":" Executive function provides inhibitory control (permissions), task switching (lifecycle), and cognitive flexibility (autonomy levels). Without executive function, an agent cannot self-regulate — it either does nothing or does everything."}]},{"id":"blk-74719","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105983","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-105984","text":" "},{"id":"spn-105985","marks":["code"],"text":"open_sentience"},{"id":"spn-105986","text":" hex package (this project)"}]},{"id":"blk-74720","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-105987","text":"OS-007: Adversarial Robustness"}]},{"id":"blk-74721","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105988","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-105989","text":" Immune system — self/non-self discrimination"}]},{"id":"blk-74722","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105990","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74723","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74725","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105991","text":"Five threat categories: prompt injection, model poisoning, side-channel,"}]}],"id":"blk-74724","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74726","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105992","text":"identity spoofing, resource exhaustion"}]},{"id":"blk-74727","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74729","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105993","text":"Detection rules per category"}]}],"id":"blk-74728","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74731","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105994","text":"Defense protocols: quarantine, circuit-break, escalate"}]}],"id":"blk-74730","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74733","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105995","text":"Integration with OS-006 for permission revocation and OS-008 for circuit"}]}],"id":"blk-74732","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74734","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105996","text":"breaking"}]},{"id":"blk-74735","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-105997","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-105998","text":" OpenSentience security module (draft)"}]},{"id":"blk-74736","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-105999","text":"OS-008: Agent Harness"}]},{"id":"blk-74737","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106000","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-106001","text":" Supervisory attentional system (Norman & Shallice 1986)"}]},{"id":"blk-74738","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106002","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74739","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74741","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106003","text":"Pipeline ordering enforcement (retrieve → route → act → learn)"}]}],"id":"blk-74740","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74743","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106004","text":"Quality gates between pipeline stages"}]}],"id":"blk-74742","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74745","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106005","text":"Sprint contracts: bounded execution with explicit goals and success criteria"}]}],"id":"blk-74744","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74747","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106006","text":"Context management: 60% threshold, compaction, Graphonomous overflow"}]}],"id":"blk-74746","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74749","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106007","text":"Generator-evaluator separation for adversarial grading"}]}],"id":"blk-74748","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74750","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106008","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implemented by:"},{"id":"spn-106009","text":" OpenSentience harness module (draft)"}]},{"id":"blk-74751","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-106010","text":"OS-009: PRISM — Protocol for Rating Iterative System Memory"}]},{"id":"blk-74752","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106011","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cognitive basis:"},{"id":"spn-106012","text":" Meta-cognition + psychometrics (Item Response Theory, signal detection theory)"}]},{"id":"blk-74753","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106013","marks":["bold"],"text":"What it specifies:"}]},{"id":"blk-74754","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74756","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106014","text":"9 continual-learning dimensions (retention, plasticity, transfer,"}]}],"id":"blk-74755","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-74757","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106015","text":"contradiction handling, etc.)"}]},{"id":"blk-74758","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-74760","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-106016","text":"4-phase evaluation loop: compose → interact → observe → reflect → diagnose"}]}],"id